# Live Calibration's spheres and their arrow keys: Sphere.ProcessCmdKey (ExtLibs/Controls/
# Sphere.cs:83-113) on the window MagCalib.DoGUIMagCalib shows (ProgressReporterSphere),
# ported in crates/mp-gui/src/config/live_magcal.rs.
#
# The claims: a sphere clicked takes the keyboard, as the UserControl it is takes the focus, and
# only that sphere turns. Left and Right add 5 degrees either way to the turn about z its next
# paint makes and Up and Down to pitch, which OnPaint sets back to zero unread; the paint each
# asks for turns the view 5 degrees more while "Rotate with each data point" is ticked
# (Sphere.cs:116-160). So, ticked, Left leaves the view where it was, Right turns it 10 degrees
# and Up 5; unticked - which the handler does for the first two spheres alone
# (ProgressReporterSphere.cs:111-115) - Left and Right turn it 5 and Down not at all.
# config.compass.livecal.viewN is the eye's bearing about z, Math.Atan2(eye.Y, eye.X), which
# OnPaint writes to the console (Sphere.cs:272), in degrees: 45 from the eye's (1, 1, 1).
#
# Against tests/gui/legacy-vehicle.py: a copter as ArduPilot before 4.0 was, without
# COMPASS_PRIO1_ID, so Initial Setup lists the older Compass page (InitialSetup.cs:200-207), and
# without the COMPASS_CALIBRATION capability, so the page shows its Mission Planner group and
# Live Calibration (ConfigHWCompass.cs:51-70). It sends no magnetometer readings: the window's
# loop keeps no sample, adds no point, and the views move for the keys alone.
#
# Run as: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-compass-livecal-keys.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5790

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup python3 tests/gui/legacy-vehicle.py --work $WORK --port 5790 --compass

screen params
window 1600x1200
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.
budget 14
# 14: 12.3 s measured headless on lavapipe (2026-10-16), the rule's ceiling plus one.
expect vehicle.count > 0
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92).
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok
click param-download
expect params.held 18

click tab-setup
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigHWCompass
expect setup.page ConfigHWCompass
expect config.compass.active true
expect config.compass.class ConfigHWCompass
expect config.compass.legacy.enabled true
expect config.compass.legacy.mpcalib true
expect config.compass.livecal.open false

# The button: Strings.MagCalibMsg, then the window, its spheres seen along (1, 1, 1).
click compass-livecal
expect config.compass.dialog Please click ok and move the autopilot around all axises in a circular motion
click compass-dialog-ok
expect config.compass.dialog none
expect config.compass.livecal.open true
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 45.0
expect config.compass.livecal.view2 45.0
expect config.compass.livecal.view3 45.0

# The first sphere clicked, "Rotate with each data point" ticked: Right 5 and the paint's 5.
click magcal-sphere1
key Right
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 55.0
# Left's 5 back and the paint's 5 on: where it was. Up then turns it the paint's 5 alone, which
# says Left's key went through.
key Left
key Up
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 60.0
# The others did not move.
expect config.compass.livecal.view2 45.0
expect config.compass.livecal.view3 45.0

# Unticked: the first two spheres' paints no longer turn them, the third's still do.
click magcal-rotate
click magcal-sphere1
key Left
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 55.0
key Down
key Right
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 60.0
click magcal-sphere2
key Right
expect config.compass.livecal.view2 50.0
click magcal-sphere3
key Right
expect config.compass.livecal.view3 55.0
expect config.compass.livecal.view1 60.0
